### 4.1 Positive Consequences
- Streamlined deployment model (single self-contained binary or container).
- Direct developer transparency with clear failure modes.

### 4.2 Negative Consequences / Trade-offs
- Requires disciplined handling of local file persistence and backup procedures.

## 5. Pros and Cons of Considered Options
### Option A
- Good: Tight integration with existing standard library patterns.
- Bad: Requires explicit internal queue polling instead of managed cloud messaging.

### Option B
- Good: Fully managed cloud infrastructure.
- Bad: Introduces operational cost, latency, and vendor lock-in.

